 The fetch script downloads and verifies Git blob hashes for the Antmicro PDM microphone-board PCB, schematic, project, design rules, and Apache-2.0 license from a pinned Copperbench commit. See `examples/antmicro_microphone/SOURCE.txt` after fetching. The board request adds small `F.SilkS` text within the outline. KiCad's missing upstream symbol/footprint libraries may produce **pre-existing** warnings; BoardGuard checks for new violations rather than requiring a clean report.
 
+KiCad DRC/ERC commands have a **180-second per-command timeout** by default. Override it for larger designs in PowerShell with `$env:BOARDGUARD_KICAD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = "240"`. The validator inherits the current OS/user environment so KiCad can find its normal configuration and library paths. If validation still times out or produces an invalid report, BoardGuard refuses to proceed.
+
 On the build machine, `kicad-cli` was absent and package installation timed out. Real ERC/DRC execution has therefore **not been verified here**. If validation was blocked by an unavailable tool, install KiCad then retry the same request ID with `boardguard resume antmicro-add-label-001 --request examples/requests/antmicro_add_silk.json --backend kicad --approve`.
 
 ## Safety and execution model
